---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Heading from '../Heading.astro';
---

<Section id="packages" tone="paper-2" labelledby="packages-title">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[540px_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-[100px]">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Heading id="packages-title">Packages for the software you run</Heading>
      <p class="text-[17px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2 md:text-[19px]">
        The library covers databases, observability, networking, and applications, with more packages added all the
        time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-9">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-t border-line pt-6">
        <h3 class="text-[22px] font-semibold md:text-[26px]">Growing the library</h3>
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2 md:text-[17px]">
          We use an established agent-assisted process to build new packages quickly and test each one against a range
          of test clusters we operate.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-t border-line pt-6">
        <h3 class="text-[22px] font-semibold md:text-[26px]">Helm charts work too</h3>
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2 md:text-[17px]">
          You can use existing Helm charts with Kix. They let you bring in software you already use, though they do not
          provide every benefit of a native Kix package.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
